WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.912
To close, the decisions
and who makes them.

2
00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:07.066
The CISO signs off the mover
proof and owns drift severity

3
00:00:07.066 --> 00:00:10.626
and every finding, while HR
fixes every wrong value.

4
00:00:10.626 --> 00:00:13.338
The executive sponsor sets the wave plan,

5
00:00:13.338 --> 00:00:16.850
and identity engineering
calls each wave's go or no-go.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.716
A population's cutover is signed by HR,

7
00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:23.600
the identity owner, the ISSO
and the business owner.

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.592
The GCC question needs a named owner
and a date, a reorganization's release

9
00:00:28.592 --> 00:00:33.338
is agreed in advance, and every
destructive step gets its own approval.

10
00:00:33.338 --> 00:00:38.420
The checklist fits in three lines: one
mover proved with no ticket; waves by

11
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.837
query with seven days of proof and the
tree archived; drift closed at the source.

12
00:00:43.837 --> 00:00:48.437
Next, take each track's own guide,
and the project plan for the dates.

13
00:00:48.437 --> 00:00:51.376
Make the attributes
true, and keep them true.

14
00:00:51.376 --> 00:00:52.200
Thank you.
